  T3 and T4 in detail (canonical footing, F = 1.819).
    GROWTH.  The g-cancellation in the source is exact, so the boost does NOT drive growth directly.  What moves
    growth is the background normalisation the closure forces, and the two consistent normalisations push it in
    OPPOSITE directions -- so growth alone does not uniquely kill the model, and both readings are reported:
      (a) measured H0, Omega_Lambda forced to 0.234 : sigma_8 in [0.822, 0.924] -- ENHANCED (the universe is 57% matter, so rho_m/rho_tot is larger)
      (b) h refitted to the acoustic scale                : sigma_8 in [0.812, 0.942]
      (c) rho_Lambda held, H0 floats                      : sigma_8 in [0.722, 0.811] -- SUPPRESSED (the source is LambdaCDM's exactly, so only the extra friction (1/2) dln g/dln a acts)
      best RSD Delta chi^2 over every (z_t, W) and every construction: +0.00 on 7 f*sigma_8 points (gate <= +9.00)
    EXPANSION.  At the measured H0, Omega_Lambda = 1/F - Omega_m - Omega_r = 0.2343 is
    (z_t, W)-INDEPENDENT: g(a = 1) = F is fixed by the clusters, and closure at a = 1 does not know when the roll
    happened.  The transition parameters cannot buy it back.  The three constructions, all offered to the model:
      (a) H0 = 67.36 fixed, densities CMB-fixed : Omega_Lambda = 0.2343 (measured 0.685); d(theta_*) -5.08% to +27.69% (gate 0.30%, Planck 0.030%); BAO Delta chi^2 -1.8 to +1072.9;
          q0 -6.218 to -0.139 (SNe -0.55 +/- 0.10); SNe rms 0.002-0.171 mag -- 25/3645 pass
      (b) h refitted, acoustic scale exact      : H0 = 51.0-90.0 km/s/Mpc where a root exists (2641/3645 have NO root at any h: the acoustic scale is unreachable);
          there Omega_m = 0.177-0.549 and Omega_Lambda = 0.000-0.373 (measured 0.315, 0.685), BAO Delta chi^2 -1.8 to +425.7 -- 63/3645 pass
      (c) rho_Lambda held, H0 floats            : H0 = sqrt(F) x 67.36 = 90.9 km/s/Mpc, against 67.4-73.0 measured -- 0/3645 pass
      the gate allows the whole band H0 = 60-80 km/s/Mpc, which brackets Planck and SH0ES with margin.
    NOT GATED, reported because it is real and adverse: a rolling G also drifts the type-Ia absolute magnitude,
    M_B propto -(15/4) log10 G through the Chandrasekhar mass -- 0.97 mag across the transition,
    against a ~0.03 mag systematic floor.  Including it makes T4 strictly worse; it is left out to keep the gate
    favourable to the model.  Likewise the SNe check marginalises over an absolute offset, which is favourable.

