============================================================================================================================
  T7 -- the fork (requirement 5): MODEL B, the enhancement in the PERTURBATIONS ONLY
============================================================================================================================
    MODEL B is a strictly WEAKER and DIFFERENT model, labelled as such wherever it appears.  The background
    expansion is held exactly LambdaCDM while the Poisson source is multiplied by g(a).  That is the
    phenomenological mu(a) parametrisation, not a completion: no action is supplied for it here, and the
    background gravitational effect of the rolling field has to be cancelled by hand.  It evades BBN and the
    expansion history BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by passing them, so only CMB, growth and delivery have content.
    canonical F = 1.819: sigma_8 spans [0.811, 11.777] (LambdaCDM 0.8111); 276/3645 models pass CMB + growth + delivery
      SURVIVING REGION (MODEL B): z_t in [0.01, 0.5148], W in [0.02, 0.5224]; there sigma_8 in [0.813, 0.853], Delta chi^2_RSD in [+0.4, +9.0]
    alt       F = 1.681: sigma_8 spans [0.811, 7.840] (LambdaCDM 0.8111); 353/3645 models pass CMB + growth + delivery
      SURVIVING REGION (MODEL B): z_t in [0.01, 0.6026], W in [0.02, 0.5922]; there sigma_8 in [0.813, 0.856], Delta chi^2_RSD in [+0.3, +8.9]
  [PASS] T7 [fork B] the weaker perturbation-only model survives its applicable gates (CMB, growth, delivery at the cluster redshifts)   (canonical: 276/3645, alt: 353/3645)

  what MODEL B still owes -- stated rather than closed; it is NOT claimed here to be a live mechanism:
    (i)   no action.  A G that gravitates perturbations but not the background is not a scalar-tensor theory; the
          Bianchi identity ties the two and the cancellation must be inserted by hand.  L6's ordering argument was
          defeated here only by the ROLL, and the roll is a BACKGROUND statement.  MODEL B keeps the roll's evasion
          while discarding the roll's background cost, which is exactly why it survives -- and why that survival
          should not be read as a result until an action produces it.
    (ii)  lensing versus dynamics.  MODEL B enhances the dynamical potential by F at cluster outskirts.  If the
          lensing potential is enhanced equally it is a pure G rescaling and inherits every background constraint
          above; if it is not, cluster lensing and hydrostatic masses must disagree by of order F, and they are
          observed to agree to tens of percent.  That gate is not run here.
    (iii) galaxies.  A time-only g(z) is spatially uniform, so MODEL B still needs the SAME screening L6 excluded
          in order to keep galaxies at G_0.  The roll relaxes only L6's BBN-ordering horn, never its OVERLAP horn
          (clusters and galaxies at identical baryon density requiring enhancements 12.8 sigma apart).  MODEL B
          therefore inherits L6's overlap kill unchanged.
    Two further doors this script does NOT close, stated: a NON-MONOTONE g(z), which is a fitted history rather
    than a roll; and a rolling coupling that is not a rescaling of G but an extra clustering component, which is
    dark matter and is closed elsewhere in the programme, not here.

============================================================================================================================
  how robust is the T6 verdict?  the surviving region is set by the GROWTH gate, so vary it and report
============================================================================================================================
    The gate as preregistered is Delta chi^2_RSD <= 9 (3 sigma).  Neither loosening nor tightening it is done to
    reach a preferred answer; both are shown so the reader can see where the boundary is.
                       growth gate |                    canonical |                          alt
      Delta chi^2_RSD <= 4  (2 sigma) |     0/3645 of the coarse grid |     3/3645 of the coarse grid
      Delta chi^2_RSD <= 9  (3 sigma, THE GATE) |    21/3645 of the coarse grid |    48/3645 of the coarse grid
      Delta chi^2_RSD <= 16 (4 sigma) |    47/3645 of the coarse grid |    76/3645 of the coarse grid
      Delta chi^2_RSD <= 25 (5 sigma) |    63/3645 of the coarse grid |    77/3645 of the coarse grid
    The surviving models sit AT the top of the growth gate on every footing, so the T6 PASS is a boundary result,
    not a comfortable one -- and it is reported as a PASS because the gate was fixed before the scan, not after.

============================================================================================================================
  T8 -- the gate this lane's escape was never going to help with, asked and quantified
============================================================================================================================
    L6 killed the screened force on TWO independent horns.  The roll was invoked against the first (the
    cosmological ordering: the background must be at least as unscreened as cluster outskirts, forcing
    G_cosmo/G_local >= 1.82 at BBN), and against that horn it works -- T1 passes exactly and by construction.
    The SECOND horn is untouched by any cosmological history: clusters and SPARC galaxies OVERLAP COMPLETELY in
    baryon density yet require enhancements differing at 12.8 sigma, and at the same acceleration clusters need
    2.2-5.1x the boost galaxies are measured to have (L2, L6 -- this lane's own committed results).  That is a
    SPATIAL contrast between two populations observed at essentially the SAME EPOCH.  A g(z) is spatially
    uniform, so the only contrast it can supply between them is the difference in their redshifts.
    SPARC's own redshifts, from the committed catalogue: 175 galaxies, distances 0.98-127.8 Mpc, median 16.5 Mpc (Hubble flow at h = 0.6736)
      => z_gal = 0.00371 (median), 0.0287 (most distant); clusters z = 0.047-0.090
    canonical: over the T6-surviving models, the roll gives clusters g(z_cl)/g(z_gal) = 0.9266-0.9640 relative to galaxies
    alt      : over the T6-surviving models, the roll gives clusters g(z_cl)/g(z_gal) = 0.9331-0.9749 relative to galaxies
    The requirement is 2.2-5.1.  The roll supplies at most 0.9749 -- and because g DECREASES with
    redshift while clusters sit at HIGHER redshift than the galaxies, the sign is WRONG: the roll makes clusters
    slightly LESS enhanced than galaxies, not more.  It is short by a factor of 2.3-5.2.
  [FAIL] T8 [inherited] the roll ALSO supplies the cluster-versus-galaxy contrast, so the spatial screening L6 excluded on its overlap horn is no longer needed   (it supplies 0.9749 against a required 2.2-5.1, in the wrong direction; the two populations are observed 0.0037 < z < 0.090 apart and no g(z) can separate them. So a T6 PASS clears the COSMOLOGICAL gates only: the model still needs exactly the density-screening L6 excluded at 12.8 sigma, which the roll never addressed)

  SUMMARY OF THE PARAMETER SPACE (canonical footing, F = 1.819, 3645 models scanned):
    BBN alone               :  3645/3645   z_t in [0.01, 3000], W in [0.02, 5]
    CMB alone               :  3038/3645   z_t in [0.01, 995.1], W in [0.02, 5]
    growth alone            :  1509/3645   z_t in [0.01, 3000], W in [0.02, 5]
    expansion alone         :    63/3645   z_t in [0.01, 0.3208], W in [0.4064, 0.6714]
    delivery alone          :  3259/3645   z_t in [0.01, 3000], W in [0.02, 5]
    growth+exp, same constr.:    21/3645   z_t in [0.01, 0.3208], W in [0.4064, 0.5224]
    BBN+CMB+delivery        :  2652/3645   z_t in [0.01, 995.1], W in [0.02, 5]
    ALL FIVE (MODEL A)      :    21/3645   z_t in [0.01, 0.3208], W in [0.4064, 0.5224]
    MODEL B, its own gates  :   276/3645   z_t in [0.01, 0.5148], W in [0.02, 0.5224]

============================================================================================================================
  THE VERDICT OF THIS LANE, as the pair (T6, T8)
============================================================================================================================
  T6 PASSES.  The roll does what L6 said it might: because g(z_BBN) = 1 exactly while g(0) = F, the
  cosmological-ordering horn that closed the screened force is genuinely evaded, and a narrow region of
  (z_t, W) then survives BBN, the CMB, the growth of structure, the expansion history -- acoustic scale, q0,
  the SNe distance-modulus shape and the absolute BAO ladder -- and still delivers the enhancement at the
  redshifts where the clusters are measured.  It survives on ONE construction, (b): h refitted so the acoustic
  scale matches exactly, giving H0 near 68-72 km/s/Mpc with Omega_Lambda near 0.25-0.32.  What makes that
  possible is that the roll's own dln g/dln a term in H(z) partly MIMICS dark energy, so a universe that is
  about half matter by energy density can still reproduce the observed distances.  This is the first mechanism
  in this programme to reach the cluster residual without being excluded by the gate it was proposed against.
  It is a BOUNDARY result and is reported as one: every survivor sits at the top of the growth gate (best RSD
  Delta chi^2 +5.3 canonical, +3.1 alt, against a gate of +9), with sigma_8 = 0.85-0.86 and f(0) = 0.57-0.64
  against LambdaCDM's 0.527.  Tightening the growth gate from 3 sigma to 2 sigma empties the canonical footing
  entirely and leaves 3 models of 3645 on the alt one.

  T8 FAILS, and it is the decisive half.  L6 closed the screened force on TWO horns and the roll addresses only
  one.  The other is that clusters and galaxies overlap completely in baryon density while requiring
  enhancements 12.8 sigma apart -- a SPATIAL contrast between populations observed at z = 0.004 and z = 0.09.
  A spatially uniform g(z) supplies a factor 0.93-0.97 between those epochs, in the WRONG direction, against a
  required 2.2-5.1.  So the late-time transition buys the cosmology and not the mechanism: it still needs the
  density-dependent screening that L6 excluded, and it does not weaken that exclusion by anything.

  Stated as an open door rather than a closure: the surviving cosmology is a real object worth naming.  A model
  with G_cosmo/G_local rolling to about 1.7-1.8 since z ~ 0.1-0.4 is not cosmologically excluded on these gates,
  and it predicts sigma_8 = 0.85-0.86 with H0 = 68-72 -- a sharp, falsifiable pair that current RSD already
  strains and the next generation of growth measurements will settle.  What it does NOT do is explain clusters.

RESULT: 1 FAIL -> ['T8 [inherited] the roll ALSO supplies the cluster-versus-galaxy contrast, so the spatial screening L6 excluded on its overlap horn is no longer needed']
